{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My lesson shall drop as the rain.</b> This is the testimony that you shall testify — that I say before you the Torah I gave to Israel, which is life for the world, like this rain which is life for the world (cf. Sifrei); as the heavens drip dew and rain." "<b>Shall drop.</b> A term of dripping, and likewise (Psalms 65) ״יִרְעֲפוּן דָּשֶׁן״, (Deuteronomy 33) ״יַעַרְפוּ טָל״." "<b>Shall distil as the dew.</b> Because everyone rejoices in it, since rain causes distress to people — such as wayfarers, and one whose vat is full of wine (Sifrei)." "<b>As the small rain.</b> A term of storm wind, as the Targum renders ״כְּרוּחֵי מִטְרָא״ — just as these winds sustain the grasses and make them grow, so words of Torah make those who learn them grow." "<b>And as the showers.</b> Drops of rain. It appears to me that it is called רְבִיב because it shoots like an arrow, as you say ״רֹבֶה קַשָּׁת״ (Genesis 21)." "<b>Dew.</b> ארברי\"ץ, the covering of the earth when it is clothed in green." "<b>Tender grass.</b> A single stalk is called עֵשֶׂב, and each and every species individually is called עֵשֶׂב."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {5 "the la'az is Old French herberie, 'herbage / green growth'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:11.166165635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}